{"Title":"An Act relative to protective custody","BillNumber":"S1270","DocketNumber":"SD52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T12:51:05.82"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"BET0","Name":"Bruce E. Tarr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/BET0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T12:51:05.82"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1270/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Tarr, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1270) of Bruce E. Tarr for legislation relative to protective custody.  Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 9A of Chapter 111E as inserted by section 1 of chapter 161 of the acts of 2020 is hereby amended by inserting in the first sentence of the second paragraph after \"immediately obtaining appropriate emergency medical treatment\" the following:-provided such custody shall continue in force and effect for the duration of necessary transport, screening and evaluation for treatment\r\n\tSECTION 2. Section 9A of Chapter 111E as inserted by section 1 of chapter 161 of the acts of 2020 is hereby amended by inserting at the end of the third paragraph after the word \"treatment\" the following:-and evaluation \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J18","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J18"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}